jobResponsibilities:
(i)	Accelerating the adoption of advanced BE technologies through a variety of levers (e.g. innovation, grants, procurement, regulations) so that we can build better and build faster;
(ii)	Monitoring the health and capacity of the BE sector to meet our development needs, and engendering a pro-enterprise environment for our BE sector to thrive; and
(iii)	Developing a strong core of local capabilities and talents as we embark on more complex and challenging projects, as well as projects in emerging areas (e.g. coastal protection).
(iv)	Recalibrating our foreign worker policies so that the construction sector has access to the necessary manpower while managing possible disamenities and taking good care of our foreign workforce; 

The officer can expect a rigorous and rewarding experience that will sharpen highly transferrable skills in policy analysis, balancing trade-offs, stakeholder management, scheme design, data analysis, public communications, amongst others. 

The officer will also gain exposure to a variety of policy domains including foreign and local manpower policies, industry development, technology and innovation, procurement policies, legislation etc.

The Income Security Policy Division (ISPD) drives national efforts to empower Singaporeans in achieving greater financial security in retirement. Within ISPD, the Retirement System Department lead policies to help Singaporeans meet retirement, housing and healthcare needs through the Central Provident Fund (CPF) system. 

Your work will directly impact how Singapore’s evolving workforce, including platform workers and self-employed persons, build their retirement savings. You will also work closely with agencies such as CPF Board, Ministry of Finance (MOF), Ministry of Health (MOH), Ministry of National Development (MND) to shape policies affecting housing, healthcare, and retirement adequacy for Singaporeans. This role offers exposure to Singapore’s wider social security landscape, where you will learn to translate data insights into policies that balance competing priorities and public expectations.
You will have the opportunity to work on the following: 
• Analyse workforce trends and CPF contribution patterns to design retirement policies for Singapore's evolving workforce;
• Propose policy solutions, from behavioural nudges to government support, to better help platform workers and self-employed persons grow their retirement savings;
• Drive reviews to optimise the use of CPF savings for housing and healthcare needs, while safeguarding long-term retirement adequacy; 
• Oversee the full policy process from scheme design, stakeholder consultations to implementation and public comms; and
• Engage in efforts to streamline the collection of CPF contributions, so as to improve the employer and employee experience for businesses and Singaporeans.

You can also look forward to a collaborative and nurturing working environment, with supervisors supporting your career development.

jobDescription:
The Municipal Services Office (MSO) was set up in Oct 2014 to improve the coordination, delivery and quality of municipal services by Government and Town Councils. These services include the upkeep and improvement of common areas in public and private estates, and the upgrading or provision of facilities and infrastructure.

The next bound of municipal service delivery involves:
i. ramping up of forward intelligence capabilities powered by AI-driven predictive analytics to enable foresight planning and support the development of pre-emptive operations;

ii. deploying AI-enhanced data focused tools (e.g. dashboards, regular data reports and AI-powered analytics tools) to increase the productivity of officers across the municipal sector and to support them in making data-driven policy decisions;

iii. humanising the digitalisation of government services (e.g. OneService Chatbot) for an optimised, resident-centric experience.

jobResponsibilities:
In this role, you will:

•	Develop national and sectoral strategies to secure the resilience of Singapore’s supply chains for essential and critical goods and services, and to mitigate and withstand impact from external shocks; 

•	Analyse and synthesize findings on critical sector supply chains, challenges and needs;

•	Build the division’s collaboration network with key stakeholders across the Government, industry and academia; 

•	Strengthen supply chain intelligence and analysis capabilities.

jobRequirements:
Requirements

•	Excellent writing, communication, interpersonal and presentation skills;

•	Able to work independently as well as in teams, and across multiple workstreams;

•	Aptitude for policy design, systems and analytical thinking, in order to deal with complex problems and recommend actionable solutions;

•	Possess a driven and self-starter attitude as well as resourcefulness in solving problems; 

•	Good stakeholder management skills dealing both with internal and external stakeholders; and

•	Data analysis skills including data visualisation and the ability to extract insights from complex datasets.

•	Proven relevant experience as a Personal Assistant, or in a similar role supporting senior management; 
•	Able to work independently with good organisational and time-management skills to provide support in secretarial matters relating to assigned principal; 
•	Work with relevant stakeholders at various levels to obtain relevant inputs and ensure smooth coordination and transition between meetings and appointments; 
•	Professional and resilient, able to perform under pressure, manage short timelines and adapt to fast-paced environment with shifting priorities quickly.

Applicants are required to have:

•	At least 5 years of work experience in one or more of the following areas: public policy, government affairs, international engagement, foreign policy; 

•	Experience working in China, or a China-focused role, preferably involving engagements with Chinese officials; 

•	Strong command of written and spoken Chinese;

•	Excellent interpersonal and networking skills; and

•	Experience in organising visits, meetings and events for senior executives and/or government officials.

jobResponsibilities:
Legal Associates are critical team members in the Ministry who render civil legal advice, instruct on the amending of legislation and work on policy matters with a heavy legal content. You can expect a fulfilling career in the public sector and be involved in pioneering the development of Singapore employment law (e.g. workplace fairness and platform workers legislation). Your functions and duties include the following:

• Rendering legal advice on issues under the Ministry’s purview (including employment law, trade unions, industrial relations, workplace safety and health, work injury compensation, foreign manpower and administrative law (including judicial review) and WTO international law); 
• Advising on legal issues in cases dealt with by the Ministry, such as on foreign manpower issues, work compensation, workplace fairness etc;
• Reviewing, drafting and vetting legislation administered by the Ministry;
• Collaborating with the Ministry’s policy divisions on legal policy projects;
• Drafting, vetting and rendering advice on contracts, data disclosure agreements and MOUs; and 
• Conducting training on contemporary legal topics.

METI’s Energy and Carbon (E&C) Cluster leads initiatives to reduce emissions and drive the transition to a low-carbon economy, while ensuring energy security and cost-competitiveness, and enabling Singapore to sustain economic growth. Officers in this cluster develop energy and carbon markets, plan energy infrastructure, build Singapore’s capabilities to harness low-carbon energy sources, and manage emission trajectories and carbon budgets. You will collaborate with stakeholders across Government, industry, and international partners to support sustainable economic transformation and green growth through strategic planning, policy analysis, and partnerships.

The Carbon Strategy Division within the E&C Cluster takes the lead in cross-cutting policymaking to decarbonise our economy and meet our Net Zero targets, while maintaining our economic competitiveness.

We are looking for driven and capable officers who (i) thrive in a fast-moving environment, (ii) have a keen interest in carbon, energy and economic transition policy, and (iii) are adept at working with multiple stakeholders within and outside the public sector. In particular, the officer will be responsible for one or more of the following workstreams:

(a) Developing strategies for national mitigation measures, leveraging carbon tax implementation and the deployment of the Carbon Mitigation Programme Budget;

(b) Leading the development of industry decarbonisation policies, through the development of effective incentive schemes and other levers;

(c) Overseeing R&D efforts into longer-term industry decarbonisation pathways.

jobRequirements:
The candidate should be equipped with the following competencies:
• Possess strong analytical skills, and be able to provide policy recommendations by drawing on a wide variety of sources;
• Have a keen interest in the development and deployment of policies and technologies that can support Singapore’s Net Zero ambitions;
• Be very comfortable working with a wide range of stakeholders, both within and beyond the public service, which requires strong interpersonal, organisational and communication skills;
• Possess the ability to work well both independently and as part of a team;
• Be driven, meticulous and resourceful;
• Candidates with relevant experience in policy-related work (particularly in the public sector), and sustainability and energy-related fields will be assessed favourably.

